{"name":"Cherry Blossom","hex":"#f5c1d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherry blossom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The blossom or flower of the cherry tree, particularly the Japanese cherry (Prunus serrulata).","A stylized depiction of the blossom of the cherry tree, as used in Japanese mon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry_blossom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry blossom","blocks":[{"text":"The cherry blossom, or sakura, is the flower of trees in Prunus subgenus Cerasus. Sakura usually refers to flowers of ornamental cherry trees, such as cultivars of Prunus serrulata, not trees grown for their fruit. Cherry blossoms have been described as having a vanilla-like smell, which is mainly attributed to coumarin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg/330px-Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_blossom"},{"title":"Cherry Blossom (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Blossom is the fifth studio album by the British pop rock band the Vamps. It was released on 16 October 2020 via EMI Records, and includes the single \"Married in Vegas\". The album debuted atop the UK Albums Chart, becoming the Vamps' second number-one album in their home country. It is promoted by a concert tour that begun on 6 September 2021."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/21/The_Vamps_-_Cherry_Blossom.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Blossom_(album)"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"},{"title":"Blossom","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, blossoms are the flowers of stone fruit trees and of some other plants with a similar appearance that flower profusely for a period of time in spring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png/330px-Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blossom"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg/500px-Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg/1280px-Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg/500px-Prunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prunus speciosa (Oshima cherry), a species of cherry tree that has given rise to many cultivars[15][16]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrunus_speciosa_in_the_Jardin_des_Plantes_002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/%E3%82%AB%E3%83%B3%E3%82%B6%E3%83%B3%E5%85%A8%E4%BD%93.jpg/500px-%E3%82%AB%E3%83%B3%E3%82%B6%E3%83%B3%E5%85%A8%E4%BD%93.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c